 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 241863,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/e8fcc31e6f8eac89.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Sverre E. Kjeldsen, et al./Hypertension, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>Platelets are small cell fragments present in blood which play a role in blood clotting. The graph shows a research study on the effect of the hormone epinephrine on the platelet count in blood. The epinephrine IV part of the graph shows where epinephrine was injected into the blood sample. Consider the ACD line and ignore the EDTA line in the graph.</p>\n<p>Which option describes the effect of epinephrine on platelet count?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 756914,
     "content_html": "Epinephrine increases platelet count in a J-shaped curve."
    },
    {
     "id": 756915,
     "content_html": "Epinephrine increaes platelet count in an S-shaped curve."
    },
    {
     "id": 756913,
     "content_html": "Epinephrine causes an initial spike ine platelet count. After the spike, platelet count drops even when epinephrine injection continues."
    },
    {
     "id": 756912,
     "content_html": "Epinephrine causes an initial spike ine platelet count. After the spike, platelet count remains constant as long as epinephrine injection continues."
    }
   ],
